<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Luhansk</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Voroshilovgrad</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Luhansk is a city in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/donbas">Donbas</a> region of eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ukraine">Ukraine</a>, which grew around a state iron foundry established in 1795. It became an industrial centre of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coal">coal</a> mining, metalworking and locomotive building, and was called Voroshilovgrad for much of the Soviet era. Since 2014 it has been held by Russian-backed forces, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> claimed to annex the region in 2022.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/luhansk.jpg" alt="Luhansk" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Qypchak · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:East_Spire_House.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
